preConditionHook:
// Brooks's middle-of-the-day, middle-of-the-range caution, price half only:
// the close sits within middleZoneFraction of the session's range of that
// range's midpoint. Placed NEGATED it is the "trade only away from the
// middle" filter; placed plain it selects the chop.
//
// The source is a composite of a clock window and this price test. The clock
// half IS TimeWindow, already in the corpus, and the entry pane ANDs, so only
// the price half is carried here.
//
// Not RangeMidpointZone, which bands the midpoint of a FIXED N-bar window,
// and not CloseRangePosition, which places the close inside its OWN bar. The
// window here is the session so far: it grows through the day and resets at
// the open, so no setting of rangeLookback reproduces it.
//
// Direction-agnostic, so both sides are identical text.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)). Intraday bars only.
// The test is written multiplied, never as a ratio, so a session whose high
// equals its low fires on both sides rather than dividing by zero (EL raises
// a runtime divide-by-zero on a zero denominator).
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    sessHigh = high[0];
    sessLow = low[0];
} else {
    if (el_gt(high[0], sessHigh)) sessHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], sessLow)) sessLow = low[0];
}
sessMid = (sessHigh + sessLow) / 2;
